--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT SHIPPED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI ExportsPage at web parity: a pure @Observable
state holder (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) over an injectable
ExportsDataSource seam whose value types mirror the web `ExportJobSummary` 1:1
(production binds the KMP export endpoints GET /export/jobs + POST
/export/jobs/bulk through the seam). Export-job metadata is control-plane data —
it carries NO SI units, so there is no unit conversion (the ADR display-boundary
rule is N/A here, like the sibling GDPR Export / Feature Flags pages). There are
no charts and no map (manifest declares 0/0).

The page reproduces the web chrome (PageContainer title + subtitle), the
bulk-action toolbar (web `BulkActionToolbar`), and the single web `GlassPanel`
(GlassPanel1) that hosts the export-jobs table:

  GlassPanel1 — the export-jobs list. Faithful to the web, the panel ALWAYS
    renders and switches its OWN data state in place (loading skeletons / error +
    Retry / empty / the table) rather than gating the surface. The adaptive table
    (ExportsPage.Table.swift) is a columnar Grid on macOS/iPad regular width and
    per-row cards on compact iPhone — the master select-all checkbox (tri-state:
    none/some[indeterminate]/all), per-row selection, Type, Format (uppercased),
    Size (formatBytes), Created (formatDateTime), the status Badge tinted by
    statusVariant, and the per-row Download link for `ready` jobs.

  Bulk toolbar — shown above the panel only when a selection exists (web
    `count > 0`): the selected count + pluralized noun (one/other), a destructive
    Delete routed through a HIG `.confirmationDialog` (title + body + the
    `common.delete` confirm), and a Clear action.

Files (all under apps/apple/Sources/Features/Exports/, + the test):
  ExportsModels.swift          — ExportsJobStatus (tolerant wire-fold + tone),
                                 ExportJobSummary value type, ExportBulkResult/
                                 ExportBulkFailure, ExportsDataSource seam +
                                 SampleExportsDataSource, exportDownloadUrl(),
                                 ExportsFormat (formatBytes / formatDateTime).
  ExportsPageModel.swift       — @MainActor @Observable model: list state,
                                 bulk selection (web useBulkSelection contract:
                                 toggle / select-all tri-state / clear / prune),
                                 deleteSelected, download URL derivation.
  ExportsPage.swift            — the View: chrome, bulk toolbar + confirm,
                                 GlassPanel1 with the 4-state switch, previews.
  ExportsPage.Table.swift      — the adaptive Grid/cards table + a11y.
  ExportsRouteRegistration.swift — registers `.exports` into the shell registry.
  Tests/Unit/Features/Exports/ExportsPageModelTests.swift — 32 unit tests.

Navigation: AppRoute gains `.exports` (pathSegment "exports" → web /exports,
Operations group, icon arrow.down.doc.fill); TeslaSyncApp registers
ExportsRouteRegistration so the NavigationSplitView/TabView shell renders the
page and the deep link resolves (AppRouteParser already maps /exports via the
route's pathSegment).

Type names: the page-local domain status enum is `ExportsJobStatus` (NOT
`ExportJobStatus`) — the latter already exists as the Dashboard
ExportStatusWidget's 4-case enum; the exports-list union needs 5 states
(queued/processing/ready/failed/expired) so it is a distinct, prefixed type.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DATA SOURCES (bound through the @Observable model; web hook names kept at call sites)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  useExportJobs       -> ExportsDataSource.loadJobs()            (GET  /export/jobs)
  useBulkExportsDelete-> ExportsDataSource.bulkDelete(ids:)      (POST /export/jobs/bulk)
  exportDownloadUrl   -> exportDownloadUrl(_:) free function     (/api/v1/export/jobs/{id}/download)
  Optimistic delete reproduced (web `bulkDelete.mutateAsync(ids)` → `sel.clear()`):
  deleted rows are dropped locally, the selection cleared, an emptied list folds to
  the empty state; on failure the selection is preserved for retry (web mutation
  branch). Selection is pruned to present ids on every (re)load.

